        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Normalize BOM and CRLF line endings in skill frontmatter parsing",
        "summary": "The `parseFrontmatter` function in `common/src/util/parse-skill.ts` now strips leading byte-order marks and converts carriage-return/line-feed pairs to Unix line endings before the YAML engine parses the content. This normalization prevents the `yaml` library from retaining carriage returns in the final frontmatter value, a behavior that previously caused skills saved on Windows to fail name validation and be silently dropped during loading. The change ensures that CRLF and BOM variants of a skill document parse identically to their LF-only counterparts.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `common/src/util/parse-skill.ts`, the `parseFrontmatter` function now normalizes input by stripping a leading BOM and converting CRLF line endings to LF before passing the string to `gray-matter`, as shown in the hunk replacing `matter(content, MATTER_OPTIONS)` with `matter(content.replace(/^\\uFEFF/, '').replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n'), MATTER_OPTIONS)`.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not detail the specific Windows user workflow that triggered the discovery of this line-ending mismatch, though a comment references a Discord help request from 2026-11-08.",
