      "facts": [
        "A side chat's turn (history-store.ts `openSideChat`): read-only, with no Freebuff tools, because its parent's agent is working in the same folder. A Desktop without it refuses the request (the schema is strict), never running a side chat with write access.",
        "A side chat (`openSideChat`): the chat it was opened beside, or null for an ordinary chat. Side chats are left out of `listChats`. Absent from older servers.",
        "Open a side chat beside a chat on the computer it runs on: a fork, read-only and hidden from chat lists, made from the chat's last saved turn even while a turn runs. Deleting it (or its parent) discards it. `chatId` is minted by the client and reused on a retry.",
        "The ids of the turns a side chat copied from its parent start with this; its own turns' never do (they are client-minted UUIDs). Its panel shows only its own.",
        "This native build runs a side chat's turns read-only (`readOnly` on `harness_start`), so the chat menu offers Side chat on its chats. Older builds omit it.",
        "(the schema is strict), never resuming the source's session in two chats."
      ],
